INT. COUNTY PAROLE OFFICE - OPEN-PLAN DESK AREA - DAY

Cubicles, a dying ficus, a laptop propped on a stack of case files. Officer DANA REED sits on a Zoom call. On screen, Dan Reyes, 40s, sits in a kitchen, mug in hand.

ON SCREEN (SLACK): #parole-team - Gus: reminder, Reyes check-in at 2, pls be nice

DANA
Dan, thanks for logging in. Three months clean, nice work.

DAN (V.O.)
Thanks, Officer Reed. Job's going good. Warehouse hired me full time.

DANA
Great. And the ankle monitor is charging overnight?

DAN (V.O.)
Every night. Plugged in by the bed.

DANA
Good. And you haven't been near Fulton Street?

DAN (V.O.)
No, ma'am. Not once.

Across the room Officer GUS PARRA's monitor BUZZES. He frowns, leans in, and goes pale.

ON SCREEN (SLACK): Gus: Dana. DANA. Pull up his GPS. Now.

DANA
(reading, still smiling at the camera)
Dan, can you hold your mug a little closer to the screen?

DAN (V.O.)
Sure.

Behind him, through the window, a street sign. FULTON ST. A door SLAMS somewhere in the office.

DANA
Interesting kitchen.

DAN (V.O.)
Officer Reed, I can explain.
